	<annotations>
		<text id="0" type="text/markdown" rect="(40, 30, 380, 60)" font-family="Helvetica" font-size="14">**Lab 2: Data Exploration and Processing**  
auto-mpg.csv, 398 cars</text>
		<text id="1" type="text/markdown" rect="(690, 110, 260, 90)" font-family="Helvetica" font-size="14">**Step 1: Explore**  
Load the file and look at it with a table, statistics and three plots.</text>
		<text id="2" type="text/markdown" rect="(120, 590, 230, 80)" font-family="Helvetica" font-size="14">**Step 2: Create Class**  
car_make = FORD, CHEVY, VW or OTHER, from model_2.</text>
		<text id="3" type="text/markdown" rect="(1020, 170, 290, 100)" font-family="Helvetica" font-size="14">**Step 3: Impute**  
Fill in the 6 missing horsepower values, then pull out just those 6 cars to compare the methods.</text>
		<text id="4" type="text/markdown" rect="(1330, 500, 250, 110)" font-family="Helvetica" font-size="14">**Step 4: Outliers**  
Find the outlier in displacement vs mpg, look it up, then let the Outliers widget flag it.</text>
		<text id="5" type="text/markdown" rect="(1400, 760, 240, 110)" font-family="Helvetica" font-size="14">**Step 5: Lper100k**  
New column for litres per 100 km, a scatter plot against horsepower, and save to csv.</text>
		<text id="6" type="text/markdown" rect="(120, 950, 300, 80)" font-family="Helvetica" font-size="14">**Step 6: Distributions by make**  
Reload the saved csv with car_make as the target.</text>
		<arrow id="7" start="(690, 190)" end="(600, 240)" fill="#1F77B4" />
		<arrow id="8" start="(300, 670)" end="(390, 690)" fill="#1F77B4" />
